    "username": "sama",
    "nickname": "奥特曼",
    "text": "As part of the October 6 release we had a particularly clean advance on the matrix multiplication exponent, with a new upper bound of 9/4. Since then, the model has been working on a LOWER BOUND for this exponent. This is already pretty crazy since NOTHING was known for lower bounds! Today we announced that actually 9/4 is tight ... This is really the kind of result that I never thought I would see in my lifetime.\n\n(btw, by an \"old\" result of Yin Tat Lee and collaborators this also implies that linear programs can be solved in time n^{9/4}.)",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://x.com/SebastienBubeck/status/2125402576145572334",
    "time": "2026-11-25 09:33",
    "created_at": "Wed Nov 25 01:33:56 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2125402576145572334",
    "is_retweet": true
  },
  {
    "username": "sama",
    "nickname": "奥特曼",
    "text": "We’re now testing Private Inference, our latest offering as part of OpenAI Private Intelligence, with a small group of customers.\n\nStronger privacy protections will make frontier AI useful for a lot more work, and business privacy is important for a healthy ecosystem. Reach out to @shekar4x if interested!\n\n(Also, ZDR with Private Safety Processing enables automated safety reviews without giving OpenAI personnel access to the underlying content.)",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://x.com/sama/status/2125638790593274259",
